Problem Statement
Given an array containing only 0s, 1s, and 2s, sort the array in ascending order
Example:
nums = [2, 0, 2, 1, 1, 0]
Output: [0, 0, 1, 1, 2, 2]


Brute Force : Sorting
Code:
class Solution {
public:
    void sortColors(vector<int>& nums) {
        sort(nums.begin(), nums.end());
    }
};

Complexity
Time: O(n log n)
Space: O(log n)


Better Solution : Counting
Idea
Since there are only three possible values:
Count how many 0s are present.
Count how many 1s are present.
Count how many 2s are present.
Then overwrite the array:
Put all the 0s first.
Then all the 1s.
Then all the 2s.

Code:
class Solution {
public:
    void sortColors(vector<int>& nums) {

        int count0 = 0;
        int count1 = 0;
        int count2 = 0;

        // Count 0s, 1s and 2s
        for (int num : nums) {
            if (num == 0)
                count0++;
            else if (num == 1)
                count1++;
            else
                count2++;
        }

        // Put 0s
        int index = 0;

        while (count0--) {
            nums[index++] = 0;
        }

        // Put 1s
        while (count1--) {
            nums[index++] = 1;
        }

        // Put 2s
        while (count2--) {
            nums[index++] = 2;
        }
    }
};

Complexity
Time: O(n)
Space: O(1)
